  "summary": "The paper evaluates a 4‑qubit variational QNN and a hybrid quantum transfer learning (QTL) model for credit default prediction on a Kaggle dataset (32,580 samples). The standalone QNN achieves 0.8097 accuracy and AUC 0.7446, while the hybrid QTL model improves to 0.9117 accuracy and AUC 0.9134 with minority‑class recall increasing from 0.16 to 0.73. All experiments run on the PennyLane default.qubit simulator with no real quantum hardware.",
